<title>USA: IPO FILING-Blazer Energy Corp.</title>
<headline>IPO FILING-Blazer Energy Corp.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name		 Blazer Energy Corp</p>
<p>NYSE Stock symbol		N/A</p>
<p>Estimated price range	   N/A</p>
<p>Total shares to be offered    3.1 million shr</p>
<p>Shrs outstanding after ipo    17,500,000</p>
<p>Lead Underwriter    Merrill Lynch &amp; Co</p>
<p>Underwriters over-allotment  465,000 shrs</p>
<p>Note: Blazer is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Ashland Inc and upon completion of the offering, Ashland will own about 82.3 percent of the outstanding common. Business: Blazer, based Houston, Tx., is an independent energy company engaged in the exploration for and the development, production, acquisition and marketing of natural gas and oil in the United States and in Nigeria. Use of Proceeds: Net proceeds will be used to pay the $180 million cash portion of the previously declared $195.4 million Ashland Dividend.</p>
<p>Financial Data in 000s year ended Sept 30:</p>
<p>				   1996		 1995</p>
<p>   - Revenue		$304,071	    $190,293</p>
<p>   - Net Income	    $75,361		$9,919</p>
